<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Xie of Zhou</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Prince Yuchen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Xie of Zhou, personal name Yuchen, was a rival king set up after the fall of the Western Zhou capital in 771 BCE, in opposition to King Ping. Supported by the Duke of Guo and other lords, he ruled for some years at Xie, but around 750 BCE Marquis Wen of Jin killed him, leaving King Ping as the sole Zhou king. He is known mainly from the Bamboo Annals and the Xinian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a>.</p></div>
